.TH SDL_OpenHapticFromJoystick 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_OpenHapticFromJoystick \- Open a haptic device for use from a joystick device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_haptic.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Haptic * SDL_OpenHapticFromJoystick(SDL_Joystick *joystick);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
You must still close the haptic device separately\[char46] It will not be closed with the joystick\[char46]
.PP
When opened from a joystick you should first close the haptic device before closing the joystick device\[char46] If not, on some implementations the haptic device will also get unallocated and you\(aqll be unable to use force feedback on that device\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I joystick
the
.BR SDL_Joystick
to create a haptic device from\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a valid haptic device identifier on success or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CloseHaptic (3),
.BR SDL_IsJoystickHaptic (3)
